{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/misotokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(cs)NSObject"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(pl)NSObject","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s7CVarArgP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SQ","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SH","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a elevation semantic token none,","        \/\/ with values depending to color scheme. These values are defined as elevation raw tokens.","        let bottom_0 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y0, blur: blur0, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack0)","        let bottom_1_100 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y100, blur: blur200, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack100)","","        \/\/ Then the develoment team declares an \"higher\" level elevation semantic token","        \/\/ inside ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside BlueCoatTheme+ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens extension","        \/\/ ElevationCompositeSemanticToken is a typealias for MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken to keep same grammar as design kit","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(light: bottom_0, dark: bottom_1_100)","        }","","        \/\/ If the same elevation is used whatever the color scheme is","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(bottom_0)","        }"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated elevation semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level elevation semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone.","","        @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","        @Environment(\\.colorScheme) var colorScheme","","        \/\/ Given you want to apply the elevation token \"raised\"","        var body: some View {","            \/\/ Apply the token of elevation for the shadow effect without managing yourself the color scheme","            Rectangle()","                .shadow(elevation: theme.elevations.raised))","        }"]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ Or get the token depending to the color scheme and do whatever you want with","    theme.elevations.raised.elevation(for: colorScheme)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The case of this "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},{"type":"text","text":" is quite particular because in fact it contains "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},{"type":"text","text":" (i.e. raw tokens) instead of semantic tokens."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In fact only the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"color"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of the elevation effect vary depending to the color scheme,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but in the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"text","text":" kit this is composite raw tokens which are defined for ligh and dark mode as only one token."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 0.8.0"}]}],"name":"Since"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"symbolKind":"class","externalID":"c:@M@MISOTokensSemantic@objc(cs)MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","role":"symbol","title":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","modules":[{"name":"Tokens for semantics"}],"roleHeading":"Class"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(light:dark:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/dark","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/light"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/elevation(for:)","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/isEqual(_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","t